WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.467
-As you guys know,
we're always striving

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.300
to get better here at
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.934
♪ Harder, better,
faster, stronger ♪

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:11.534
[ Laughter ]
So before every show,

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.868
we put out a suggestion box
for the audience just to get

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:15.734
some feedback about what
you guys think of the show,

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.634
things that you'd like to see us
do, that kind of stuff.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:20.467
So tonight, let's look inside
the "Audience Suggestion Box."

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.400
Here we go.
-♪ Look into the box ♪

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.300
♪ The suggestion box ♪

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.467
-Okay, here we have --
The first one is from Julia Gee.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:33.167
Said, "Hey, Jimmy, I'm so
excited for 'House of Gucci'

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.367
to come out this weekend.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.734
Are you going to go see it?"

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.667
Absolutely. I can't wait.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:38.701
How about you, Quest?

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.434
-Yeah, man. I love the costumes.
Yeah.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:41.834
-Yeah. How about you, Mark?

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.334
-I'll probably go. Adam Driver
is good in everything.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:45.901
-Yeah, he was good. Yeah.
What about you, James?

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.834
Are you excited for
"House of Gucci"?

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.400
-Never heard of it.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:58.234
♪♪
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:01.400
-Wow!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.634
-Sorry I asked.
-Wow.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:06.200
-This next one is
from Jeff Billingham.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.133
"Hey, Jimmy,
I'm a big fan of tennis."

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.000
Oh, good. I like tennis too.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.234
"But I don't like it when tennis
players make those loud grunts.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.501
Please don't show me
a bunch of other sports

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.868
with tennis grunting in it.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.701
It would just really
bum me out."

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.000
"Just kidding.
It's opposite day."

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.100
It's a very tricky suggestion.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.334
Well, if it's opposite day
and you don't want to see

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:30.801
grunting in other sports,
here you go, bud!

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.434
[ Grunting ]

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:35.100
[ Grunting ]

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:36.801
[ Grunting ]

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.667
[ Grunting ]

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.300
[ Grunting ]

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:46.033
[ Grunting ]

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.501
[ Grunting ]
-There you go.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.033
[ Applause ]

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.334
It's opposite day.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:56.234
-Alright, here we go.
Let's try one more here.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:59.400
This one is from April Sing.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.067
"Hey, Jimmy, I want to make hand
turkeys with my kids this year,

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.767
but I'm a little self-conscious
about my big hands.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:06.934
Any tips?"

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.467
There's nothing wrong with
having big hands.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:10.033
Bigger the turkey, the better.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:13.801
To show you, we're about to make
the world's largest hand turkey.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.334
Let's roll out the paper.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:23.234
♪♪

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:31.167
♪♪

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.133
Alright, let's set
the world record. Go ahead.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.934
-Ready?
-Yeah.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:42.100
♪♪

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.767
Sorry, I'm drawing your hair.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.300
Alright. Did you get it, Hig?

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.000
Alright, you guys can get up
now.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.200
Thank you very much.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.734
Let's see what we did.
Let's see what we did.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.667
[ Drumroll ]
Oh, wow!

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:54.801
Wow! Look at this.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.601
It's a masterpiece.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.000
World's largest hand turkey.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.067
Just missed a couple things
just to make sure it's complete.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.467
That is unbelievable
right there.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.067
There you have it,
a world record.

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:12.133
World's largest hand turkey
right there.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.667
I'm putting this on the fridge.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.400
Thank you, everybody.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:21.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.701
That was fun.

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:26.767
We gotta call
the Guinness people.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.934
This next one here is
from Dahlia Lopez.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.100
"Hey, Jimmy, my favorite part of
football games

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.934
is the touchdown celebrations.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:36.100
What would you do
if you scored a touchdown?"

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.234
Well, that's a good question.
You know, I'm old-fashioned.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.634
I'd probably just go through the
classic spiking the football.

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:42.133
How about you, Quest?

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.834
-I kinda like a Lambeau Leap,
you know?

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.667
Where you jump into the crowd.
-Yeah, I like that.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.300
That's a good one. Yeah.
What about you, Higs?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.501
-I don't know. Maybe -- Maybe
something like this.

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:52.567
[ Grunts ]

00:03:53.767 --> 00:04:00.300
♪♪

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:06.767
♪♪

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:10.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.534
-That was amazing!

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.033
Higgins, that was amazing.

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:15.701
-Yeah, whatever.

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:18.901
-Wow.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.467
Higgins, I didn't know you knew
how to catch a football.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:22.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.767
-I had to learn that.
I knew the break dancing.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:28.434
-Yeah. Alright, last suggestion
right here.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.033
This is from Chelsea Mitchell.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.934
"Hey, Jimmy, I love Hallmark
Christmas movies,

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:34.167
but I've noticed their posters
are all really similar.

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:36.434
You should do some re-creations
of them."

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:39.000
Yeah, that's a great idea. But
I'm going to need a little help.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.868
So here to join me in
re-creating Hallmark's Christmas

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.567
movie posters is Julie Bowen!

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:47.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.701
Ah, now that's what I'm talking
about.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:50.367
-Let's do this.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.501
I appreciate this. Yeah.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:54.167
Alright.
-Let's do it. Come on.

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:58.534
-We're going to do many of these
as we can as fast as we can.

00:04:58.534 --> 00:05:00.267
-Competitive dressing.
-Thank you, Steph.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.067
Yep.
-Okay.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.200
-Alright, here we go.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.133
Now, the original poster
will pop up on the left.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:08.300
We're going to have
to re-create it.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:09.868
Are you ready to do this?
-Hell yeah.

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.033
Are we making out
in any of them?

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:13.000
-I don't know. I have no idea.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.567
Here we go. Ready?
Alright, let's do it.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:16.701
And go.

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:19.767
Oh!

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.767
[ Ding! ]
-Oh, look at this.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.200
Candy cane.

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.701
Oh, wrong way?
[ Applause ]

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.133
No, wrong way.
It was the wrong way.

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:33.601
We went the wrong way.

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:35.234
-No, we were right.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:38.868
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:41.133
-Oh!
-Here on this side.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:43.934
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:51.767
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.400
-We did it. We did it.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.100
-Oh, that one?
-Oh, wait.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.634
-Am I here?

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:58.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.267
[ Ding! ]
-We nailed that.

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:01.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:05.334
[ Ding! ]

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:07.868
I like your bland face.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:09.534
-Oh.

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:10.934
[ Laughter ]
[ Ding! ]

00:06:10.934 --> 00:06:12.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.234 --> 00:06:14.367
Oh.

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:17.334
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:19.801 --> 00:06:22.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.667 --> 00:06:24.067
[ Dinging ]
-There you go!

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:26.133
We have it right there!
Thank you very much!

00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:27.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:29.267
Oh, wow!
Oh, who's a -- Come on.

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:31.000
Thank you.
-We killed it.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.934
-The best. Thank you.
That is Julie Bowen right there.

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:35.634
That is all the time we have
for our suggestion box.

